    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Empire Records: The Soundtrack is a 1995 various-artists compilation tied to the cult film about a day in the life of a struggling independent record store, and its 2026 reissue returns one of the era’s most recognizable alternative-rock soundtracks to vinyl. Issued by A&M Records, it captures the mid-’90s moment when college rock, power pop, and radio-friendly alternative were converging into a highly commercial but still genuinely energetic soundtrack identity.\n\nThe album’s appeal comes from how well it mirrors the movie’s spirited, rebellious tone: standout cuts from Gin Blossoms, The Cranberries, Edwyn Collins, Toad the Wet Sprocket, Better Than Ezra, Cracker, and others make it feel less like a generic film tie-in and more like a snapshot of the alternative mainstream at its peak. Its best-known tracks, especially “Til I Hear It From You” and “A Girl Like You,” helped make the compilation a lasting favorite among fans of ’90s rock soundtracks, and the reissue underscores its continued status as a compact, culturally nostalgic document of the decade’s stage-and-screen crossover appeal.",
